    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Depth-first, forward traversal for vertices.</para><para>This traversal follows edges in their natural order from source to target visiting child vertices before siblings. The advancing methods and operators (<ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Algorithm_1_1GraphTraversal_1a574c3e3db87c283066fd908ef4ab0863" kindref="member">advance</ref>, <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Algorithm_1_1GraphVertexTraversal_1aea0f7171e8c2a2db23463dea6188bb4f" kindref="member">next</ref>, etc.) stop only at vertex enter events (<ref refid="namespaceSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Algorithm_1a4a563d6bb47e082bbe1e40bcc59e1f59a269618ed6163d346e3fdfbb93a40e1a8" kindref="member">ENTER_VERTEX</ref>). Dereferencing the traversal object returns a graph vertex node. </para>    </detaileddescription>
